Genre Core:
Dark electro-art pop × cinematic glitch ballad × cosmic industrial minimalism

Emotional Vector:
Isolation → gravitational pull → ignition → implosion glow

Tempo:
~88–94 BPM (slow pulse, heartbeat-driven)

Time Signature:
4/4, but phrasing floats over bar lines

Key Center:
D minor (with modal lift to F major in pre-chorus feel)

STRUCTURAL DNA (Layered Escalation)
1️⃣ INTRO (0:00–0:20 feel)

Single distant sub-bass tone (sine wave, filtered)
Granular cosmic texture (like radio interference from deep space)
Sparse reversed piano fragments
Whisper-close female vocal, breath-heavy, intimate, fragile
No percussion yet — just pulse swell
Atmosphere:
Cold void. A star not yet burning.

2️⃣ VERSE (minimal propulsion)
Soft electronic kick (muted, low, rounded)
Snare replaced by filtered clap with long tail
Arpeggiated synth in minor mode (thin, glassy, detuned)
Vocal layered: dry lead + ghost octave whisper
Subtle harmonic distortion on vocal peaks
Dynamic rule:
Nothing fully resolves. Every phrase feels suspended.

3️⃣ PRE-CHORUS (gravitational pull builds)
Low tom pulse introduced
Bass widens (chorus effect subtle)
Synth pad thickens with analog warmth
Harmonic shift hints at lift but never fully bright
Vocal intensity rises — slightly strained, emotional crack allowed
Tension rule:
Compression increases. Air tightens.

4️⃣ CHORUS (ignition but controlled)
Full beat engages
Distorted sub bass under clean top layer
Layered vocal harmonies bloom wide (ethereal but grounded)
High frequency shimmer (like solar flare particles)
Reverb expands dramatically then snaps back
Energy rule:
Power without chaos. Heat without explosion.

5️⃣ BRIDGE (void fracture)
Beat drops out
Glitch fragmentation of prior vocal lines
Reverse swells and metallic echoes
Pulsing low drone (like reactor core hum)
Vocal delivered nearly spoken, emotionally stripped
This is the collapse moment.
Not loud — exposed.

6️⃣ FINAL CHORUS (controlled supernova)
Beat returns heavier
Bass distortion increases
Background vocals almost chant-like
Micro-cracks in vocal allowed (authentic strain)
End with sustained note dissolving into static
Outro rule:
Fade into radio noise — star signal drifting away.

PRODUCTION TEXTURE RULES
• Analog warmth layered under digital sharpness
• No EDM drops
• No bright pop sheen
• Reverb tails long but low in mix
• Sub-bass must be felt more than heard
• Vocal remains emotional centerpiece

SONIC REFERENCES (Not copied, but tonal cousins)
Son Lux atmospheric tension
James Blake low-end intimacy
Kishi Bashi emotional layering restraint
Patrick Watson fragile vocal atmosphere

EMOTIONAL INSTRUCTION (CRITICAL)
This is not a song about brightness.
It is about distance.
The star is not warm.
It is collapsing.
The voice is both calling and disappearing.